{"type":"system","subtype":"background_tasks_changed","tasks":[{"task_id":"bvizdh5hx","task_type":"local_bash","description":"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_4\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/hypothesis.md\nRefinement of the incumbent `person_switch_ideal_pattern_rule_built` (tally span judged against a personal expected span, switching judged by closeness to a personal ideal switching rate, chunk variety and a rule-built penalty scaled by a personal pattern sensitivity, a personal left/right lean). The one change: people weigh the end of a sequence, the flips they read last, more than its interior — a sequence that finishes on a streak (the coin \"getting stuck\" at the end, HTHHTT, THTHHH) looks less random, and every flip of the final run beyond the first counts against it, by a shared terminal-streak penalty. Of two sequences with the same number of switches, people therefore pick the one that ends with a switch, addressing the critique that among equal-switch pairs people choose the sequence ending with a switch more often than the incumbent, which is blind to where switches occur, predicts.\nEOF\necho terminal_streak_recency_pattern_rule > $D/model_name.txt\npython3 - << 'PY'\nsrc = open(\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/models/person_switch_ideal_pattern_rule_built.py\").read()\nstart = src.index(\"import numpy\")\nbody = src[start:]\ndoc = '''\"\"\"Terminal-streak recency penalty on the person-specific switch-ideal rule-built judgement.\n\nRefinement of `person_switch_ideal_pattern_rule_built`: tally span judged against\na personal expected span, switching by closeness to a personal ideal switching\nrate, chunk variety and a rule-built penalty scaled by a personal pattern\nsensitivity, and a personal left/right lean. The one change: people weigh the\nflips they read last, so a sequence that ends on a streak looks less random —\nevery flip of the final run beyond the first counts against it (a shared\nterminal-streak penalty). Among equal-switch pairs people pick the sequence\nthat ends with a switch.\n\"\"\"\n'''\nbody = body.replace('''    a = sequence_a.strip().upper()''', '''    def terminal_excess(seq):\n        # Flips of the final run beyond the first (0 when it ends on a switch).\n        k = 1\n        while k < len(seq) and seq[-1 - k] == seq[-1]:\n            k += 1\n        return float(k - 1)\n\n    a = sequence_a.strip().upper()''')\nbody = body.replace('''        \"log_len\":''', '''        \"term_diff\": terminal_excess(a) - terminal_excess(b),\n        \"log_len\":''')\nbody = body.replace('''    log_len = pm.Data(\"log_len\"''', '''    term_diff = pm.Data(\"term_diff\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    log_len = pm.Data(\"log_len\"''')\nbody = body.replace('''    # Person-specific left/right''', '''    # The change: shared penalty per flip of the final run beyond the first.\n    tau = pm.Normal(\"tau\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0)\n\n    # Person-specific left/right''')\nbody = body.replace('''        + side[participant_id]''', '''        - tau * term_diff\n        + side[participant_id]''')\nopen(\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_4/candidate.py\",\"w\").write(doc+body)\nPY\ngrep -n \"term\\|tau\" $D/candidate.py\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run2/repo && timeout 1500 /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5"}],"uuid":"8e8f6e23-8c42-4d5b-9d70-088a8eaad1a7","session_id":"169b0949-9732-4c75-883e-accfe1bb7e8d"}
